{"strongs": "H1835", "word": "דָּן", "translit": "dan", "root": "דחן", "morph": "N:N--L", "pos": "proper name, masculine", "gloss": "judge", "definition": "דָּן proper name, masculine ( judge ) — 1. son of Jacob and Bilhah Gen 30:6 ; Gen 35:25 ; Exod 1:4 ; Josh 19:47 ; Judg 18:29 ; 1Chr 2:2 . 2. the tribe of Dan, מַטֵּה דָן Exod 31:6 ; Exod 35:34 ; Exod 38:23 ; Lev 24:11 ; Num 1:39 ; Num 13:12 ; Josh 21:5 ; Josh 21:23 (all P ); בְּנֵי דָן Gen 46:23 ; Num 1:38 ; Num 2:25 ; Num 7:66 ; Num 10:25 ; Num 26:42 ; Num 34:22 ; Josh 19:40 ; Josh 19:47 (twice in verse); Josh 19:48 (all P ) Judg 1:34 ; Judg 18:2 ; Judg 18:16 ; Judg 18:22 ; Judg 18:23 ; Judg 18:25 ; Judg 18:26 ; Judg 18:30 מַחֲנֵה דָן Num 2:25 ; Num 2:31 ( P ) — on Judg 13:25 ; Judg 18:12 see מַחֲנֶה ; מִשְׁפְּחֹת דָּן Num 26:42 ( P ); דָּן alone in poetry Gen 49:16 ; Gen 49:17 ; Deut 33:22 (twice in verse); Judg 5:17 , elsewhere Num 1:12 ( P ) Deut 27:13 ; 1Chr 27:22 ; 2Chr 2:13 ; Ezek 48:1 ; Ezek 48:2 ; Ezek 48:32 . 3. a city on northern frontier of Israel at one of the sources of the Jordan, originally לַיִשׁ Judg 18:29 (compare v Judg 18:7 ); = לֶשֶׁם Josh 19:47 captured by a colony of Danites; named Dan, and made a sacred place with rites of worship that lasted until the exile ( Judg 18:30 ); = Tell el Kâdî , Rob BR iii. 351, 358 Bd Pa1 265 . This place is frequently referred to: Gen 14:14 ; Deut 34:1 ; 1Kgs 12:29 ; 1Kgs 12:30 ; 1Kgs 15:20 ; 2Kgs 10:29 ; 2Chr 16:4 ; Jer 4:15 ; Jer 8:16 ; Amos 8:14 read also וּבְדָן for וְכֵן 2Sam 20:18 ᵐ5 Ew We compare Dr ; and see the phrase מִדָּן וְעַדבְּֿאֵר שֶׁבַע Judg 20:1 ; 1Sam 3:20 ; 2Sam 3:10 ; 2Sam 17:11 ; 2Sam 24:2 ; 2Sam 24:15 ; 1Kgs 5:5 given by Chronicles מִבְּאֵר שֶׁבַע וְעַדדָּֿן 1Chr 21:2 ; 2Chr 30:5 . ( Ezek 27:19 see ודן .) Note. — דָּ֫נָה יַעַן 2Sam 24:6 . As no such place is known, the text is usually regarded as corrupt, and, ᵐ5 being uncertain, is variously changed: (1) דָּ֫נָה יַעַר to Dan in the wood , Thes after ᵑ9 silvestria. (2) ( וַיָּסֹבּוּ ) דָּ֫נָה וְעִיּוֺן to Dan and Ijon Klo (compare 1Kgs 15:20 ). (3) ( סָֽבֲבוּ ) דָּן וּמִדָּן We Dr compare ᵐ5 .", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1918')\">BDB1918</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H1835')\">H1835</entry> <entry onclick=\"sn('H1842')\">H1842</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1917')\">BDB1917</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB1919')\">BDB1919</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>דָּן</bdbheb> <b>proper name, masculine</b> (<highlight>judge</highlight>) — <div class=\"point\"><b>1.</b> son of Jacob and Bilhah <ref ref=\"Gen 30:6\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"30\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"30\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(1,30,6)\">Gen 30:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Gen 35:25\" b=\"1\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"25\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"25\" onclick=\"bcv(1,35,25)\">Gen 35:25</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 1:4\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"4\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"4\" onclick=\"bcv(2,1,4)\">Exod 1:4</ref>; <ref ref=\"Josh 19:47\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"19\" vBegin=\"47\" cEnd=\"19\" vEnd=\"47\" onclick=\"bcv(6,19,47)\">Josh 19:47</ref>; <ref ref=\"Judg 18:29\" b=\"7\" cBegin=\"18\" vBegin=\"29\" cEnd=\"18\" vEnd=\"29\" onclick=\"bcv(7,18,29)\">Judg 18:29</ref>; <ref ref=\"1Chr 2:2\" b=\"13\" cBegin=\"2\" vBegin=\"2\" cEnd=\"2\" vEnd=\"2\" onclick=\"bcv(13,2,2)\">1Chr 2:2</ref>. </div><div class=\"point\"><b>2.</b> the tribe of Dan, <bdbheb>מַטֵּה דָן</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 31:6\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"31\" vBegin=\"6\" cEnd=\"31\" vEnd=\"6\" onclick=\"bcv(2,31,6)\">Exod 31:6</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 35:34\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"35\" vBegin=\"34\" cEnd=\"35\" vEnd=\"34\" onclick=\"bcv(2,35,34)\">Exod 35:34</ref>; <ref ref=\"Exod 38:23\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"38\" vBegin=\"23\" cEnd=\"38\" vEnd=\"23\" onclick=\"bcv(2,38,23)\">Exod 38:23</ref>; <ref ref=\"Lev 24:11\" b=\"3\" cBegin=\"24\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"24\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(3,24,11)\">Lev 24:11</ref>; <ref ref=\"Num 1:39\" b=\"4\" cBegin=\"1\" vBegin=\"39\" cEnd=\"1\" vEnd=\"39\" onclick=\"bcv(4,1